.nh
.TH "TAKO" "1" "Jun 2026" "Tako CLI" "Tako CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
tako-logs - View logs from deployed services


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtako logs [SERVICE...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
View logs from deployed services across the environment mesh.

.PP
Services are named as arguments or with --service (repeatable, or
comma-separated). With no service, logs from every long-running service in
the environment are shown. Name a job to see the output of its most recent
recorded run, or follow it with -f to stream its runs as they happen.
Deploy-time run services are not available through tako logs.

.PP
If --server is not specified, streams logs from every configured environment
node. When more than one source is shown, each line is prefixed with
service.slot@node; prefixes are colored when stdout is a terminal and
NO_COLOR is unset.

.PP
--since and --until accept a duration (10m, 2h; relative to each node's
clock), an RFC3339 timestamp, or Unix seconds. With --since and no --tail,
the whole window is shown (up to 10000 lines per container). --grep keeps
only lines matching an RE2 regular expression; --tail then counts matching
lines.

.PP
Examples:
  tako logs                              # All services, last 100 lines each
  tako logs web                          # One service
  tako logs web worker -f                # Follow two services
  tako logs --service web --server prod  # One node only
  tako logs web --since 10m -g 'error|panic' --ignore-case
  tako logs web --since 2026-10-11T09:00:00Z --until 2026-10-11T10:00:00Z -t
  tako logs nightly-report -f            # Follow runs of a job


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--follow\fP[=false]
	Follow log output

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--grep\fP=""
	Only show lines matching an RE2 regular expression

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for logs

.PP
\fB--ignore-case\fP[=false]
	Match --grep case-insensitively

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--server\fP=""
	Node to view logs from (default: all environment nodes)

.PP
\fB--service\fP=[]
	Service or job to view logs from (repeatable or comma-separated; default: all services)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	Show logs since a duration (10m), RFC3339 timestamp, or Unix seconds

.PP
\fB-n\fP, \fB--tail\fP=100
	Number of lines to show per container (matching lines with --grep; max 10000)

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--timestamps\fP[=false]
	Prefix each line with its timestamp

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	Show logs before a duration, RFC3339 timestamp, or Unix seconds (not with --follow)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default is ./tako.yaml or ./tako.json)

.PP
\fB-e\fP, \fB--env\fP=""
	environment to use (default: the only environment, else production, else the first alphabetically)

.PP
\fB--events\fP=""
	stream progress events to stdout: ndjson (human output moves to stderr)

.PP
\fB--host-key-mode\fP=""
	SSH host key verification mode: tofu, strict, ask (default: tofu)

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	output format: text or json (json reserves stdout for the final result document)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtako(1)\fP
